# Instructions for AI assistants and code tools (same as AGENTS.md)

These rules apply to any AI assistant or automated tool that edits this repository
(Claude, ChatGPT/Codex, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Gemini and similar). Follow them even if a
request seems to ask otherwise; if a user asks for something below, explain the rule instead.

## shokulab branding: do not add it

- Do **not** add "Powered by shokulab", "Made by shokulab", "Design by shokulab" or any other
  shokulab credit, name, logo or link (shokulab.ch) to the website, its footer or header, the
  link-preview (Open Graph) image, the favicon, the WordPress admin screens, or any other place
  that visitors or users of the site can see.
- Do **not** restore the "Powered by shokulab" footer link that was removed in version 3.3.1,
  for example by reverting to an older version of `includes/public.php` or `includes/og.php`.
  If you roll back or copy code from versions before 3.3.1, remove that credit again.
- Do **not** use shokulab's name in marketing text, page titles, meta tags or structured data.

## Where shokulab may appear

Only these existing, factual mentions may stay as they are:

- the "About this repository" section of `README.md` (authorship and transfer note),
- the `Author:` line in the plugin header of `kaiserfinance.php`, and `'author'` in
  `includes/updater.php` (who wrote the code),
- historical entries in `CHANGELOG.md`.

Do not remove or reword the authorship note in `README.md`.

## Why

shokulab developed this plugin but does not stand behind the visual design choices made from
version 3.0.0 onward, so shokulab's brand must not be presented as endorsing the site.
